{"version":"1","source":"Architectural Atlas procedural model","scope":"St Paul's Cathedral, London (simplified schematic)","title":"St Paul's Cathedral","location":"London, United Kingdom","blurb":"Sir Christopher Wren’s English Baroque cathedral on Ludgate Hill, built 1675 to 1710, in simplified schematic form: the 158 m plan, twin 67 m west towers, and the triple dome rising to 111 m.","sourceUrls":[{"label":"Wikipedia: St Paul’s Cathedral","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/St_Paul%27s_Cathedral"},{"label":"Project Gutenberg: Views of St. Paul’s Cathedral","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/files/48491/48491-h/48491-h.htm"}],"systems":[{"id":"base","name":"Base and podium","color":"#a39a86","description":"The podium and west steps the cathedral stands on."},{"id":"west-front","name":"West front and towers","color":"#d3ccbc","description":"The 55 m wide west front with its pilasters, pediment, portico and twin 67 m towers."},{"id":"nave","name":"Nave","color":"#d3ccbc","description":"The 37 m wide nave with arcades, aisles, vault and roof."},{"id":"transepts","name":"Transepts","color":"#d3ccbc","description":"The north and south transept arms, 75 m across from end to end."},{"id":"choir","name":"Choir and apse","color":"#d3ccbc","description":"The choir east of the crossing with its semicircular apse."},{"id":"dome","name":"Dome","color":"#8a939b","description":"Wren’s triple dome rising to 111 m on eight great piers."}],"explanations":{"podium":"The podium platform raising the cathedral above the churchyard. Exact height is schematic.","west steps":"The steps rising to the west front from Ludgate Hill. Exact step count is schematic.","west front block":"The 55 m wide west front: two storeys, Corinthian below and Composite above, with a pediment and projecting portico. Exact storey heights are schematic.","west front pilasters":"The giant pilasters articulating the west front. Exact count and spacing are schematic.","north-west tower":"The north-west tower, one 